WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.560
We've scraped together every vague prediction,
plot hint, and educated guess available about

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.219
the Game of Thrones prequel, in an attempt
to get a clearer picture of what to expect

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:13.780
when the highly anticipated series eventually
makes its way onto television screens.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.280
Here's what we know.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.390
Shortly after HBO greenlit the pilot, author
George R.R. Martin posted on his blog that

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.320
if he got a vote, he'd call the prequel series
The Long Night.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.900
Martin is referencing a time of great darkness
that occurred during the Age of Heroes, in

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.320
which the White Walkers invaded Westeros.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.000
They were opposed by the Children of the Forest
and the First Men, with the Night's Watch

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.880
ultimately driving them back north during
the Battle for the Dawn.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.900
Then, Bran the Builder raised the magic Wall
to protect the people of Westeros against

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.880
future invasions.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.180
However, the Game of Thrones prequel series
is shooting under the working title Bloodmoon.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.460
While this working title might be a red herring,
it may still hold a few clues.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.440
In the books, there is a legend that says
the Long Night began as a result of the Blood

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.020
Betrayal, an event in which the brother of
the empress killed his sister and took her

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.560
throne.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.360
He called himself the Bloodstone Emperor,
and his reign of terror included torture,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.840
necromancy, cannibalism, and the worship of
a black stone that fell from the sky.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.311
Calling the prequel project Bloodmoon might
be a clue that the Blood Emperor and his black

00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:19.420
stone may wind up playing a pivotal role in
the events leading up to the Battle for the

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:19.960
Dawn.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.260
In the official summary for Bloodmoon, HBO
has said that the show will take place thousands

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.950
of years before the events of Game of Thrones,
beginning toward the end of the Age of Heroes

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:34.270
and journeying through the events that led
to Westeros' quote, "darkest hour."

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.350
Martin threw out the figure of 10,000 years
on his website, with the caveat that it may

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.280
actually be only half that.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.399
Whether Bloodmoon takes place five or ten
thousand years before the start of Game of

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:48.830
Thrones, we can expect this version of Westeros
to look very different from the one we've

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:49.340
come to know.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:55.520
Central holdings like Winterfell and the Red
Keep won't be constructed, and the massive,

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.040
magical Wall that divides the North from Wildlings'
lands won't have been built yet.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.540
"The Starks have manned the Wall for thousands
of years.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.840
And you are a Stark."

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.140
Considering how far in the past this series
is thought to take place, don't expect to

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.060
see any familiar faces pop up on screen.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:18.320
While the cast of Bloodmoon may still be populated
with Starks, Lannisters, and Boltons, they

00:02:18.331 --> 00:02:22.100
won't be the ones we've come to know, love,
and hate over the eight seasons of Game of

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.620
Thrones.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.910
The single exception to this could be the
Night King, whose creation we caught glimpses

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.240
of in Game of Thrones, and who is thought
to be thousands of years old.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.640
HBO has promised that the prequel will reveal
the true origin of the White Walkers, which

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.840
means we may finally learn who he was before
he became an immortal ice being.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.660
For all its strengths, Game of Thrones was
never known for its diverse casting or racial

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.220
sensitivity.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.260
While there were some regions, like Dorne
and Essos, populated by characters of color,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.200
the people who resided in them were never
the focal point of the show.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.040
However, the casting for Bloodmoon seems to
indicate that this prequel may finally take

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.220
some steps to course correct on this issue.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.500
Four actors of color — Naomi Ackie, Sheila
Atim, Ivanno Jeremiah, and Marquis Rodriguez

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.020
— have already been cast as series regulars.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.370
Since the Westeros we've seen before has been
largely filled with light-skinned characters,

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.520
this may be an indication that this new series
could spend time in some previously underexplored

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.060
lands.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.160
Perhaps we'll finally get to see Essos through
the eyes of the people who were actually born

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.260
and raised there, or learn about new lands
as well.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.760
Poldark actor Josh Whitehouse has been cast
as the male lead of the Game of Thrones prequel,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.160
and many fans are speculating that he'll play
a member of House Stark.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.040
While there's plenty of Starks throughout
Westeros history, Whitehouse will probably

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.620
be playing Bran the Builder, the legendary
founder of House Stark who was responsible

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.960
for the construction of Winterfell.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.230
After driving the White Walkers out of Westeros
and back into the far north, the original

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.740
Bran Stark worked alongside giants and the
Children of the Forest to construct the magical

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.120
Wall that we saw so much of in Game of Thrones.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.520
If Martin's claims about the premise of the
show are to be believed, it's hard to imagine

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.440
a cinematic version of The Long Night that
doesn't include Bran the Builder.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.820
Combined with HBO's promise that this prequel
will focus on "the Starks of legend," it seems

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.840
like a no-brainer that one of its main characters
would be the most famous Stark of all.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.180
HBO's official synopsis for Bloodmoon ends
with the cryptic phrase, "It's not the story

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.000
we think we know."

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.920
That's an intriguing claim even if you only
consider the history revealed over the course

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.650
of the show, but gets downright perplexing
when you take all of Martin's novels and supplemental

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.100
materials into account.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.500
While Game of Thrones touched a little bit
on the creation of the White Walkers and the

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.820
history of Westeros, the show has never been
particularly concerned with the events of

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.960
the past, keeping its eyes fixed firmly in
the present.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.870
But when taken in conjunction with the books
and supplemental texts, there are few corners

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.900
of the Thrones universe that haven't already
been thoroughly explored.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.520
Whether you're a casual viewer of the show
or a devoted scholar of the books, prepare

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.810
for the revelations of the prequel series
to completely upend some of the histories

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:04.360
and stories we've always believed to be true.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.140
It's possible that a character that history
recorded as heroic was actually more of a

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.880
villain, or that certain events happened differently
than what we've always pictured.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.650
Naomi Watts leads the ensemble cast of Bloodmoon,
and according to HBO, she'll play a charismatic

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.160
socialite hiding a dark secret.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.120
This doesn't do much to narrow the playing
field.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.300
Game of Thrones has never had any shortage
of manipulative nobles.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.320
However, Watts' blonde hair and fair complexion
have prompted some early speculation that

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:37.280
she may belong to one of the two Great Houses
of Westeros known for their light locks — the

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.160
Targaryens or the Lannisters.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.860
The problem Watts' character being a Targaryen
is that the dragon-riding family didn't even

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.220
arrive in Westeros until a few hundred years
before the start of Game of Thrones.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.620
That places them in Valyria during the time
that the prequel will take place.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.980
While it's possible that some of the series
could be set in Valyria, it seems unlikely

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:02.420
that it will be centered around a lead character
who never even sets foot in Westeros.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:07.280
House Lannister, on the other hand, was founded
in Westeros during the Age of Heroes, after

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.700
Lann the Clever tricked House Casterly into
giving up their holding of Casterly Rock.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:12.820
"Who were your ancestors?

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:14.980
Who made your family rich?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.720
Fancy lads in silk?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.740
They were f--king cuthroats.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:21.340
That's how all the great houses started, isn't
it?"

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.760
The timing works out perfectly for Watts to
be playing one of these early Lannisters,

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.560
possibly a contemporary of Bran the Builder.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.930
And while we're used to seeing House Lannister
and House Stark constantly at war with each

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.340
other, we may finally get to see them as allies.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:40.720
One of the most common criticisms leveled
against Game of Thrones was its treatment

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.900
of its female characters, a failing that was
frequently attributed to how few women have

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.200
been involved in prominent creative roles
behind the scenes.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:53.000
Only three women have ever been credited as
writers for Game of Thrones, and only one

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.580
woman has directed an episode.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:07:00.120
That all adds up to only nine out of 73 episodes
with a woman in a major creative role.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:05.500
However, if the creative team behind Bloodmoon
is any indication, don't be surprised if this

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.000
spinoff is much more female-centric in its
storytelling.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:13.760
Not only is nearly half of the announced cast
women, but Bloodmoon is helmed by Stardust

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.100
scribe Jane Goldman.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:21.100
Her impressive resume includes writing credits
for X-Men: First Class, Kingsman, and Kick-Ass,

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.540
which shows that she's no stranger to sweeping
fantasy, intense action, and large ensemble

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.060
casts.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.660
The show has also tapped executive producer
SJ Clarkson to direct the pilot episode.

00:07:30.669 --> 00:07:34.550
Her previous work includes several shows with
predominantly female casts like Orange Is

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.240
the New Black and Jessica Jones.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:41.360
The mysterious forest-dwellers who assisted
Bran Stark in Game of Thrones will likely

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.020
get a lot more screen time in the prequel
series.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.740
In the main show, the Children were relegated
to enigmatic side characters who appeared

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:52.760
out of nowhere in season four, and then were
seemingly wiped out by season six.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:57.180
But toward the end of the Age of Heroes, the
Children played a much more prominent role

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.320
in Westeros' history.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:03.420
The Children of the Forest are inextricable
from the tales of Bran the Builder, the Battle

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.720
for the Dawn, and the construction of the
Wall.

00:08:05.949 --> 00:08:10.440
They created the White Walkers, and then ultimately
joined forces with the giants and the First

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:10.960
Men to defeat them.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:15.520
Given their importance to the time period
that the show will be set during, it's highly

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.671
probable that one or more of the announced
cast for the series will portray one of the

00:08:19.671 --> 00:08:21.120
Children of the Forest.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.760
That means that we're about to learn a whole
lot more about this secretive race.

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:31.100
One of the most notorious figures in Westerosi
history is the hero Azor Ahai, who helped

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:35.260
save the world from a great darkness while
wielding his flaming sword, Lightbringer.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:40.330
While it is not made explicitly clear in the
books whether Azor Ahai was the same figure

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.340
as the Last Hero, who lived during the Long
Night and helped defeat the White Walkers,

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.400
there's also nothing to say that it wasn't
him.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:51.360
Including Azor Ahai would give viewers many
of the things we've come to expect from Game

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.860
of Thrones: tragic love stories, reluctant
heroes, thrilling battles, and a touch of

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.400
magic.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.080
It would also be a way to include a character
familiar to the audience, without needing

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.520
to bring back any of the Thrones cast.

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:07.920
While viewers and readers have never actually
met Azor Ahai, he's been the subject of rampant

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.240
speculation for years.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:17.020
"In ancient books, it's written that a warrior
will draw a burning sword from the fire and

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.420
that sword will be Lightbringer."

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:23.740
Seeing him appear on screen would not only
provide the prequel with a rich character

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.600
to explore, but would excite fans hungry for
more information about the mysterious hero.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.640
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter
shortly before the final season of Game of

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:36.820
Thrones aired, Martin warned that the prequel
series would be very different from the Westeros

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.920
fans had grown accustomed to seeing:

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.240
"It's different.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.100
It's definitely very different.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.400
It's set thousands of years in the past.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.570
You're looking at a whole different era of
Westeros.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.760
No dragons, no Iron Throne, no King's Landing."

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.820
This is hardly surprising, given the time
period in which the prequel is set.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:58.760
Five to ten thousand years before Game of
Thrones, King's Landing hadn't been constructed,

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:03.180
and Aegon Targaryen hadn't yet been born to
build a throne out of the blades of his vanquished

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:03.700
enemies.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.940
Further, while dragons surely existed somewhere
in the world, the Targaryens wouldn't bring

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.940
the winged creatures from Valyria to Westeros
for thousands of years.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.760
Still, despite the immense differences between
the prequel and the familiar world of Game

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.950
of Thrones, Martin is still hopeful that fans
will enjoy it.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.980
We'll update you as we hear more about the
upcoming prequel series.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.060
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:29.020
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.120
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

